  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "VLocMkASL4hSkyE0Sf5KL5BWcPw=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:32:14.975Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The mechanism is a metasfresh callout dispatching a typed operation on document completion. Document completion is the ERP's own notion of a finished business fact, so the record boundary is the product's rather than an imposed one.\n\nThe recorded framing is commercial: offered as a metasfresh add-on they resell, not a competing store. For a partner whose business includes distributing metasfresh extensions, arriving as another channel is an obstacle regardless of technical merit; arriving as inventory for the existing channel is not. The distinction costs nothing technically and changes who has to be convinced.\n\nThe single lead is metas GmbH, based in Bonn and Cologne with a Romanian presence, marked \"2 \u00b7 next\". Together with the Abilian proposal \u2014 Switchboard packaged for the partner's own PaaS catalogue \u2014 it forms a small pattern in the corpus of shipping through the partner's existing distribution rather than beside it.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (1)\n\n**2 \u00b7 next**\n- metas GmbH (DE Bonn/Cologne + RO) \u2014 Mark Krake, Gesch\u00e4ftsf\u00fchrer \u00b7 https://metasfresh.com\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> metasfresh callout dispatching a typed operation on document completion \u2014 offered as a metasfresh add-on they resell, not a competing store.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:32:14.975474Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:32:14.975479Z"
    }
  },
